Android has no /tmp, so the mount of the new root tmpfs on the hardcoded /tmp
fails with ENOENT. Use the Termux tmp directory instead.

--- a/bubblewrap.c
+++ b/bubblewrap.c
@@ -3041,7 +3041,7 @@
    * that is sure to exist, that is sure to not be a symlink controlled
    * by someone malicious, and that we won't immediately need to
    * access ourselves. */
-  base_path = "/tmp";
+  base_path = "@TERMUX_PREFIX@/tmp";
 
   debug ("creating new namespace");
 
